 if-else-else (if-elif-else) control-flow is a structured control-flow in programming language that statements are put into three categories. Here is a Python program which illustrates how to use if-elif-else control-flow:

```python
fruits = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
frruit_to_evaluate = input('Enter a fruit: ')

if fruit_to_evaluate not in fruits:
  print(fruit_to_evaluate + " is not in the list.")
elif fruit_to_evaluate == "apple":
  print('You choose apple...')
elif fruit_to_evaluate == "banana":
  print('You choose banana...')
elif fruit_to_evaluate == "cherry":
  print('You choose cherry...')
else:
  print('You choose something else...')
```

In this case, you will need to run the Python interpreter for this code to run it correctly.
